| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| *Organization* | `${organization_id}` ([Open in STACKIT Portal](${organization_url})) |
| *Root Folder* | `${root_folder_name}`, `${root_folder_id}` ([Open in STACKIT Portal](${root_folder_url})) |
| *Management Project* | `${management_project_id}` ([Open in STACKIT Portal](${management_project_url})) |
%{ for area, id in network_areas ~}
| *Network Area* `${area}` | `${id}` ([Open in STACKIT Portal](https://portal.stackit.cloud/network-area/network-areas/${id}/overview?organization=${organization_id})) |
%{ endfor ~}
| *meshStack Platform* | ${display_name} (`${platform_identifier}`) |
| *Building Block Definition* | ${display_name} |
%{ for name, lz in landing_zones ~}
| *Landing Zone* ${lz.display_name} | `${name}`, folder `${lz.folder}` |
%{ endfor ~}
%{ for tag in landing_zone_tags ~}
| *Landing Zone Tag* `${tag.key}` | ${join(", ", [for v in tag.values : "`${v}`"])} |
%{ endfor ~}
| *STACKIT Project Service Account* | `${service_account_email}` |

To get a STACKIT project, create an environment on the platform ${display_name}, choose one of
its landing zones and add the building block ${display_name}. The project's tags have to fit the
landing zone tags.
%{ if playground_mode }
*Playground mode:* the platform identifier carries a random suffix, and this is not intended to be a
published platform.
%{ endif ~}
